    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 243\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 6788, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the public authorities law, in relation to salary\n      adjustments according to plan and step-ups or increments\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would remove  the  ability  of  the  Nassau  County  Interim\nFinance  Authority  (NIFA)  to include any salary adjustment, negotiated\ncost of living raise, \"step,\" or any other  salary-based  increment,  as\npart  of its wage freeze declaration, whenever it has approved the Coun-\nty's four-year financial plan.\n \n  State law authorizes the creation of Independent Control Boards,  such\nas  NIFA,  to  improve  the fiscal standing of certain local governments\nwhen necessary. The Independent Control Boards are authorized to  impose\nwage  freezes  to  restore fiscal order to a local government budget, as\nwell as to help curb avoidable increases to property  taxes.  This  bill\nwould  prohibit NIFA from imposing the wage freeze, which would cost the\nCounty approximately $17 million in the first year of implementation and\ncompound annually thereafter for every year a wage freeze  would  be  in\nplace.\n \n  Such  a  precedent-setting  alteration of NIFA's wage freeze authority\nwould likely open the door for similar statutory  modifications  to  the\nother  presently-governing  control boards in the State, and curtail the\nabilities of any new control board that may need to be  created  in  the\nfuture. For these reasons, I am compelled to veto this bill.\n \n  This bill is disapproved.                   (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
